vlib: cancel a pending adaptive switch when the next window is busy

An adaptive input node switches to interrupt state in two steps: a quiet
window marks it (VLIB_NODE_FLAG_SWITCH_FROM_POLLING_TO_INTERRUPT_MODE),
and after one more dispatch in polling state, which lets the driver
re-enable its interrupt, a quiet window switches it. A busy window in
between never cleared the mark, so the node stayed marked while polling
and any later single quiet window switched at once. A driver that arms
its interrupt in the marked dispatch (dpdk, 0024) would also keep arming
it during busy polling. Clear the mark when the window is busy.

--- a/src/vlib/main.c
+++ b/src/vlib/main.c
@@ -938,6 +938,14 @@
       {
 	u32 node_name, vector_length, is_polling;
       } *ed;
+
+      /* The switch to interrupt state needs two quiet windows in a row; a
+	 busy window in between cancels the pending switch. Drivers can then
+	 re-arm their interrupt in the marked dispatch, just before the
+	 switch. */
+      if (node->state == VLIB_NODE_STATE_POLLING &&
+	  v > nm->interrupt_threshold_vector_length)
+	node->flags &= ~VLIB_NODE_FLAG_SWITCH_FROM_POLLING_TO_INTERRUPT_MODE;
 
       if ((node->state == VLIB_NODE_STATE_INTERRUPT &&
 	   v >= nm->polling_threshold_vector_length) &&
